---
---

<section class="boundary-section">
	<div class="boundary-header">
		<span class="boundary-tag">Architectural Contract</span>
		<h2 class="boundary-title">Where the Line Is</h2>
		<p class="boundary-desc">
			Antiphony is infrastructure and an open protocol, not a monolithic SaaS app. It draws a deliberate line between what the decentralized audio protocol owns and what remains in your application layer.
		</p>
	</div>

	<div class="boundary-grid">
		<div class="boundary-card core-card">
			<div class="boundary-badge badge-core">In Antiphony Core</div>
			<ul class="boundary-list">
				<li>
					<strong>ATProto Lexicons:</strong> <code>dev.antiphony.*</code> records for portable audio posts, threaded replies, and transcripts.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Edge Audio REST API:</strong> Chunked audio upload, pre-signed URLs, and transactional post creation.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Enrichment Engine:</strong> Background ffmpeg audio rendition, peak waveform extraction, and AI transcription.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Multi-Tenancy Isolation:</strong> <code>originAppId</code> security boundaries and directional AppView federation.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</div>

		<div class="boundary-card app-card">
			<div class="boundary-badge badge-app">In Your App Layer</div>
			<ul class="boundary-list">
				<li>
					<strong>Identity & Accounts:</strong> User profiles, passwords, OAuth sessions, and handle verification stay with your app.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Product Experience:</strong> Custom player themes, distribution channels, feeds, and community rules.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Organizations & Teams:</strong> Workspaces, invite links, roles, and SaaS billing subscriptions.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Proprietary Connectors:</strong> Custom telephony integrations, broadcast feeds, and closed integrations.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	.boundary-section {
		max-width: 56rem;
		margin: var(--ap-space-16) auto var(--ap-space-12);
		padding: 0 var(--ap-space-4);
	}

	.boundary-header {
		text-align: center;
		margin-bottom: var(--ap-space-8);
	}

	.boundary-tag {
		font-size: var(--ap-font-xs);
		font-weight: 600;
		color: var(--ap-call);
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.05em;
		background: var(--ap-call-subtle);
		padding: 2px var(--ap-space-3);
		border-radius: var(--ap-radius-full);
	}

	.boundary-title {
		font-family: var(--ap-font-display);
		font-size: var(--ap-font-2xl);
		font-weight: 700;
		color: var(--ap-text-primary);
		margin: var(--ap-space-3) 0 var(--ap-space-2);
	}

	.boundary-desc {
		font-size: var(--ap-font-base);
		color: var(--ap-text-secondary);
		max-width: 42rem;
		margin: 0 auto;
		line-height: var(--ap-leading-relaxed);
	}

	.boundary-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
		gap: var(--ap-space-6);
	}

	.boundary-card {
		background: var(--ap-surface-card);
		border: 1px solid var(--ap-border-subtle);
		border-radius: var(--ap-radius-lg);
		padding: var(--ap-space-6);
		box-shadow: var(--ap-shadow-md);
	}

	.core-card {
		border-top: 4px solid var(--ap-call);
	}

	.app-card {
		border-top: 4px solid var(--ap-response);
	}

	.boundary-badge {
		display: inline-block;
		font-size: var(--ap-font-xs);
		font-weight: 700;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.04em;
		padding: var(--ap-space-1) var(--ap-space-3);
		border-radius: var(--ap-radius-full);
		margin-bottom: var(--ap-space-4);
	}

	.badge-core {
		background: var(--ap-call-subtle);
		color: var(--ap-call);
		border: 1px solid var(--ap-border-subtle);
	}

	.badge-app {
		background: var(--ap-response-subtle);
		color: var(--ap-response);
		border: 1px solid var(--ap-border-subtle);
	}

	.boundary-list {
		list-style: none;
		padding: 0;
		margin: 0;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: var(--ap-space-3);
	}

	.boundary-list li {
		font-size: var(--ap-font-sm);
		color: var(--ap-text-secondary);
		line-height: var(--ap-leading-relaxed);
	}

	.boundary-list strong {
		color: var(--ap-text-primary);
	}
</style>
